Subject: Tech: PSI 10 mbps bi-directional

Harry:

> I was at InterNet world this morning and spoke to a rep.  of PSI who
> said their cable offering was going to be 10 mbps bi-directional.

Well, I suppose that there's not too much use in debating this now,
but I still think that's marketer talk.  From the articles you posted
last night (thanks! great material!) it appears that they'll be
hooking ethernet cards right up to the "converter" box (great idea),
and since those cards implement a 10 mb ethernet standard, voila!
10 mbps bi-directional.  BUT: the important issue is the *actual*
achievable throughput in accessing remote sites you're interested
in. Hooking a thousand people up to a 10 mbps LAN (sic) lets you
claim 10 mbps network speed but you'd better hope nobody else
wants to use any of it.

Another unfortunateness I gathered from the articles you forwarded
was that this PSI/Continental project will apparently only be
available in parts of Massachusetts, which doesn't do many of us
much good... still, at least ExI will be hooked up.  The rest
of us will have AOL or Prodigy to look forward to.  Yay.

Hopefully, though, the PSI/Continental model, by virtue of its
simplicity and early implementation, will encourage others to
follow the same kind of path.  We'll see.

Interesting stuff.

